Subject: [PATCH 10/24] Test a database created where only its data file cannot
 sync against decisions 8 and 10

The header rule (implementation note 1) threw before the first durable
commit; decisions 8 and 10 anchor the header in the WAL instead. The test
now expects every commit acknowledged durable in the WAL, no failure, and a
power loss (the data file empty, written back, or with a torn header,
beside the WAL as last synced) to keep every row; it fails until the header
frame is implemented. Where nothing syncs, a durable commit is still refused
before it writes (decision 3), now also through a shared connection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
